Adding new columns that derive information from existing data or are based on domain knowledge is known as Feature Engineering. Even in relatively simple datasets, there are always new characteristics you could pull out to create a more in-depth analysis. One of the most critical skills a data scientist needs to learn is how to identify opportunities for feature engineering.
